---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqs = [
  {
    group: "About Ecosoft",
    items: [
      {
        q: "How long has Ecosoft been implementing ERP systems?",
        a: "Since 2013 — our first implementation was Raja Cycle, a Thai bicycle manufacturer. That same system is still running today, through multiple Odoo version upgrades. We have over a decade of production ERP experience in Thailand."
      },
      {
        q: "What makes Ecosoft different from other Odoo / ERPNext partners?",
        a: "Three things: we are active contributors to the OCA (Odoo Community Association) and ERPNext ecosystems — not just implementors; all our customisation is built as proper open-source modules, not quick hacks; and we treat client relationships as long-term partnerships, not one-time projects. Our oldest client relationship is over 10 years."
      },
      {
        q: "Do you work with clients outside Thailand?",
        a: "Our primary market is Thailand, and our platform expertise is deeply Thai-compliance-focused. We have worked with clients in Thailand with international operations, but we are not a general Southeast Asia ERP firm."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    group: "Odoo vs ERPNext",
    items: [
      {
        q: "Which is better — Odoo or ERPNext?",
        a: "Neither is universally better. Odoo CE has a more comprehensive module library and is particularly strong for manufacturing and sales-heavy businesses. ERPNext has superior project management and is better suited for service businesses and companies that want a more developer-friendly platform. We recommend the right one for your specific situation — we implement both."
      },
      {
        q: "Is Odoo Community Edition really free? What's the catch?",
        a: "Yes — Odoo Community Edition is released under the LGPL licence. There is no licence fee and no per-user cost. The 'catch' is that some modules are only available in Odoo Enterprise (the paid version). Ecosoft implements the Community Edition, enhanced with OCA-certified modules that cover most gaps — so most clients never need Enterprise."
      },
      {
        q: "Can I upgrade between versions without losing my customisation?",
        a: "Yes — if the customisation was built correctly. This is exactly where Ecosoft's OCA-standard development approach matters. Customisations built as proper modules survive version upgrades. Customisations built as hacks to core files do not. Raja Cycle has been upgraded through multiple Odoo major versions without losing their custom functionality."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    group: "Implementation",
    items: [
      {
        q: "How long does an ERP implementation take?",
        a: "A focused SME implementation covering accounting, inventory, purchasing, and sales typically takes 3–5 months. Manufacturing adds complexity. Government implementations with custom procurement modules typically run 6–12 months. The biggest variable is scope — and the biggest risk to timeline is scope creep during implementation."
      },
      {
        q: "What does an Ecosoft implementation include?",
        a: "Discovery and requirements analysis, system configuration, custom module development (where needed), data migration from your existing system, user training, and go-live support. We don't hand over a configured system and disappear — we stay through stabilisation."
      },
      {
        q: "Can you migrate data from our current system?",
        a: "Yes — data migration is included in all implementations. The complexity depends on your current system (SAP exports are straightforward; poorly structured spreadsheets are more work). We handle the migration scripts, cleaning, and validation."
      },
      {
        q: "Do you provide ongoing support after go-live?",
        a: "Yes — all clients are offered an annual support contract after implementation. This covers bug fixes, minor configuration changes, system monitoring, and access to the Ecosoft team for guidance. Many clients have been on support contracts for 5–10+ years."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    group: "Pricing",
    items: [
      {
        q: "How much does an Ecosoft implementation cost?",
        a: "Implementation cost depends on scope — number of modules, degree of customisation, data complexity, and number of users to train. We don't publish fixed prices because every implementation is different. See our pricing page for indicative ranges, or contact us for a scoped proposal."
      },
      {
        q: "Are there any ongoing licence fees?",
        a: "No ongoing licence fees for Odoo CE or ERPNext — these are open-source. You pay for Ecosoft's implementation services and, optionally, an annual support contract. There is no per-user cost that scales with your headcount."
      },
      {
        q: "How does your pricing compare to SAP or Oracle?",
        a: "Dramatically lower — both for implementation and for ongoing cost. NSTDA replaced SAP with Odoo in 2018 and reinvested the annual licence savings into system improvements. We can't give a universal ratio because SAP/Oracle costs vary widely, but open-source ERP consistently costs a fraction of the equivalent proprietary system."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    group: "Technical",
    items: [
      {
        q: "Where is the system hosted — cloud or on-premise?",
        a: "Ecosoft implements both. We handle hosting on cloud infrastructure (typically AWS or Azure) or on-premise at the client's data centre. Most clients prefer cloud hosting for convenience; government and financial institutions often prefer on-premise for data sovereignty."
      },
      {
        q: "What happens if Ecosoft closes down?",
        a: "Nothing catastrophic — because the software is open-source and the customisation is yours. You have the source code to the platform and to all custom modules. Any competent Odoo or ERPNext developer can pick up where we left off. This is a deliberate design decision, not an accident."
      },
      {
        q: "Can we integrate ERP with our existing systems?",
        a: "Yes — both Odoo and ERPNext expose comprehensive REST APIs. Ecosoft has built integrations with e-commerce platforms, logistics APIs, banking feeds, government portals, and custom line-of-business applications. Integration complexity is scoped during discovery."
      },
    ]
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ — Frequently Asked Questions | Ecosoft"
  description="Answers to common questions about Ecosoft, Odoo, ERPNext, implementation timelines, pricing, and open-source ERP for Thai businesses."
>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:2rem;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Resources</p>
      <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        Honest answers to the questions we hear most often — about Ecosoft, our platforms,
        implementation, and what open-source ERP actually costs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ GROUPS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width:860px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:3rem;">
        {faqs.map((group) => (
          <div class="faq-group">
            <h2 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">{group.group}</h2>
            {group.items.map((item) => (
              <details class="faq-item">
                <summary class="faq-question">
                  {item.q}
                  <span class="faq-chevron">›</span>
                </summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                  <p>{item.a}</p>
                </div>
              </details>
            ))}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Still have questions?</h2>
      <p>Talk to a consultant directly — we'll give you a straight answer, even if it means telling you that ERP isn't the right solution yet.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Ask Us Directly</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .faq-item summary { list-style: none; }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
</style>
